---
import Icon from "../../../common/Icon.astro";
import { LEGAL_EMAIL } from "../../../../lib/legal";

/*
 * The contact form. The white half of the card in section 2.
 *
 * BUILT TO THE SUPPLIED DESIGN, on Fredrick's instruction of Aug 28 2026 — heading, four
 * fields, placeholders and a filled Send Message button, as drawn.
 *
 * THREE DEPARTURES FROM THE BUILD BRIEF, ALL ON THAT INSTRUCTION, and each is worth
 * knowing because each was a brief rule with a reason attached:
 *
 *   1. FOUR FIELDS, NOT THREE. The brief says three and "do not add company", on the
 *      grounds that every additional field costs submissions. "Practice Name" is that
 *      company field. IT IS THE ONE FIELD NOT MARKED REQUIRED, which is the cheapest way
 *      to keep the cost down: a visitor with no practice name can skip it and still send.
 *   2. THE MESSAGE LABEL NAMES A FIRM. "…in your firm right now?" is written for a
 *      practice, and /contact is the general contact page — the site's stated audience is
 *      businesses at roughly $500k–$5M revenue, most of which are not firms. A reader who
 *      is not a firm has to translate the question before answering it. Flagged, and built
 *      as drawn.
 *   3. THE SUBMIT BUTTON IS PRIMARY FILL. The brief made secondary "a design-system rule,
 *      not a preference", but that rule existed to stop it competing with the booking
 *      button beside it. THE BOOKING BUTTON IS GONE, so this is now the only action on the
 *      page and filling it is correct. The rule was not broken; the thing it protected
 *      stopped existing.
 *
 * ONE THING THE DESIGN DOES NOT SHOW AND THIS BUILDS ANYWAY: the privacy line under the
 * button. The page collects a name, an email address and a message, and the brief called
 * that sentence CASL work rather than decoration — it is the visible statement that
 * writing to us does not become consent to be marketed at, and it is the only link to
 * /privacy at the point of collection now that the "what to expect" section is gone.
 * Dropping it would be a compliance regression rather than a design simplification. It is
 * one quiet line and it is easily removed if Fredrick wants it gone.
 *
 * NETLIFY FORMS, honeypot only, NO reCAPTCHA — reCAPTCHA loads a Google script that would
 * need a Privacy row and would have to sit behind the consent gate, at which point the
 * form breaks for anyone who has not accepted cookies.
 *
 * SUBMITTED THROUGH fetch so the panel is replaced in place rather than redirecting to a
 * thank-you page that would need building, keeping out of the sitemap, and would put a
 * second page_view against one enquiry. WITHOUT JAVASCRIPT this is still a real form and
 * Netlify still receives it.
 *
 * SESSION RECORDING: these are the site's first real input fields. Clarity masks inputs in
 * every masking mode and that cannot be switched off, but the standing rule from the
 * analytics release is that masking is VERIFIED in a recording before a form ships.
 */
---

<div class="form-panel">
  <h2 class="form-panel__heading">Start the conversation</h2>

  <form
    class="form-panel__form"
    id="contact-form"
    name="contact"
    method="POST"
    data-netlify="true"
    data-netlify-honeypot="bot-field"
  >
    <input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="contact" />

    {/* The honeypot. Off-screen rather than display:none so a bot still finds it in the
        markup, aria-hidden so a screen reader never meets it, and tabindex -1 so a
        keyboard cannot reach it — filling it silently discards the message. */}
    <p class="form-panel__honeypot" aria-hidden="true">
      <label>
        Don&rsquo;t fill this in if you&rsquo;re human
        <input type="text" name="bot-field" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
      </label>
    </p>

    <div class="form-panel__row">
      <div class="form-panel__field">
        <label class="form-panel__label" for="contact-name">Name</label>
        <input
          class="form-panel__input"
          id="contact-name"
          name="name"
          type="text"
          placeholder="Jane Doe"
          autocomplete="name"
          required
        />
      </div>

      <div class="form-panel__field">
        <label class="form-panel__label" for="contact-practice">Practice Name</label>
        {/* Deliberately not required — see note 1 in the header. */}
        <input
          class="form-panel__input"
          id="contact-practice"
          name="practice"
          type="text"
          placeholder="Acme Law Firm"
          autocomplete="organization"
        />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="form-panel__field">
      <label class="form-panel__label" for="contact-email">Email</label>
      <input
        class="form-panel__input"
        id="contact-email"
        name="email"
        type="email"
        placeholder="jane@example.com"
        autocomplete="email"
        required
      />
    </div>

    <div class="form-panel__field">
      <label class="form-panel__label" for="contact-message">
        What&rsquo;s the biggest administrative bottleneck in your firm right now?
      </label>
      <textarea
        class="form-panel__input form-panel__textarea"
        id="contact-message"
        name="message"
        rows="5"
        placeholder="Briefly describe your challenge…"
        required></textarea>
    </div>

    {/* role="alert" so it is announced the moment it appears — a message placed above a
        button is invisible to someone who has just pressed that button and cannot see. */}
    <p class="form-panel__error" id="contact-error" role="alert" hidden>
      <span class="form-panel__term">That didn&rsquo;t send.</span> Email{" "}
      <a class="form-panel__email" href={`mailto:${LEGAL_EMAIL}`}>{LEGAL_EMAIL}</a>{" "}
      directly and it will reach us.
    </p>

    <button class="form-panel__submit" type="submit">
      <span>Send Message</span>
      <Icon name="arrowRight" size={18} class="form-panel__submit-icon" />
    </button>

    <p class="form-panel__consent">
      What you send is used to answer you and nothing else. We don&rsquo;t add you to a
      mailing list. See our <a class="form-panel__link" href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
  </form>

  <div class="form-panel__success" id="contact-success" role="status" hidden>
    <p class="form-panel__success-title">Thank you &mdash; that&rsquo;s arrived.</p>
    <p class="form-panel__body">
      A person will reply, usually within one business day.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
  const form = document.getElementById("contact-form") as HTMLFormElement | null;
  const success = document.getElementById("contact-success");
  const error = document.getElementById("contact-error");

  form?.addEventListener("submit", async (event) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    error?.setAttribute("hidden", "");

    const submit = form.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(".form-panel__submit");
    const label = submit?.querySelector("span");
    const original = label?.textContent ?? "";
    if (submit && label) {
      submit.disabled = true;
      label.textContent = "Sending…";
    }

    try {
      /* Netlify accepts the post at any path on the site as long as the body carries
       * `form-name`. Posting to the page's own URL keeps it same-origin, so nothing here
       * is a third-party request and none of it is gated by consent. */
      const response = await fetch(form.getAttribute("action") || window.location.pathname, {
        method: "POST",
        headers: { "Content-Type": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" },
        body: new URLSearchParams(new FormData(form) as unknown as Record<string, string>).toString(),
      });

      if (!response.ok) throw new Error(String(response.status));

      form.setAttribute("hidden", "");
      success?.removeAttribute("hidden");
      /* Move focus to the confirmation. Without this a keyboard or screen-reader user is
       * left focused on a button that no longer exists, with nothing announced. */
      success?.setAttribute("tabindex", "-1");
      (success as HTMLElement | null)?.focus();
    } catch {
      error?.removeAttribute("hidden");
      if (submit && label) {
        submit.disabled = false;
        label.textContent = original;
      }
    }
  });
</script>

<style>
  /* Larger than the aside's heading, matching the design: this is the page's working
   * title now that the hero has handed off. */
  .form-panel__heading {
    font-family: var(--ark-font-display);
    font-size: 2.125rem;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--ark-ink);
  }

  .form-panel__success-title {
    font-family: var(--ark-font-display);
    font-size: var(--ark-h3);
    line-height: var(--ark-lh-h3);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--ark-ink);
  }

  .form-panel__body {
    margin-top: 14px;
    font-size: var(--ark-body);
    line-height: var(--ark-lh-body);
    color: var(--ark-body-ink);
  }

  .form-panel__term {
    color: var(--ark-ink);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .form-panel__form {
    margin-top: 30px;
  }

  .form-panel__honeypot {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .form-panel__row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 20px;
  }

  .form-panel__field + .form-panel__field,
  .form-panel__row + .form-panel__field {
    margin-top: 20px;
  }

  .form-panel__label {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    font-size: var(--ark-small);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ark-ink);
  }

  /*
   * Filled and borderless, per the design — the fill is the affordance.
   *
   * The transparent border is not decoration: it holds the box's size so the focus state
   * can colour it without the field growing by 2px and nudging everything below it.
   */
  .form-panel__input {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 15px 16px;
    font-family: var(--ark-font-body);
    font-size: var(--ark-body);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ark-ink);
    background: var(--ark-stage-warm);
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    border-radius: var(--ark-radius-sm);
  }

  /* --ark-muted, not --ark-muted-2: placeholder text is small text and needs 4.5:1, and
   * muted-2 measures 3.67 on this fill. */
  .form-panel__input::placeholder {
    color: var(--ark-muted);
  }

  .form-panel__textarea {
    resize: vertical;
    min-height: 132px;
  }

  .form-panel__input:focus-visible,
  .form-panel__submit:focus-visible,
  .form-panel__link:focus-visible,
  .form-panel__email:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--ark-olive);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  /* PRIMARY FILL. Correct here, and only here, because the booking button that this used
   * to sit beside no longer exists — see note 3 in the header. */
  .form-panel__submit {
    margin-top: 28px;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    padding: 17px 26px;
    font-family: var(--ark-font-body);
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--ark-on-dark);
    background: var(--ark-olive);
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    border-radius: var(--ark-radius-sm);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background-color 0.15s ease;
  }

  .form-panel__submit:hover:not(:disabled) {
    background: #2c401f;
  }

  .form-panel__submit:disabled {
    cursor: default;
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .form-panel__submit-icon {
    flex: none;
  }

  .form-panel__error {
    margin-top: 22px;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    font-size: var(--ark-small);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ark-body-ink);
    background: var(--ark-gold-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--ark-gold-border);
    border-radius: var(--ark-radius-sm);
  }

  .form-panel__error[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .form-panel__consent {
    margin-top: 20px;
    font-size: var(--ark-small);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ark-muted);
  }

  .form-panel__link,
  .form-panel__email {
    color: var(--ark-olive);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .form-panel__success[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .form-panel__success:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--ark-olive);
    outline-offset: 4px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .form-panel__heading {
      font-size: 1.75rem;
    }

    .form-panel__row {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 20px;
    }

    .form-panel__submit {
      width: 100%;
      justify-content: center;
    }
  }
</style>
